GitOps Monitoring & Observability

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing my GitOps learning journey after completing Ansible, today I’m exploring Monitoring & Observability in GitOps 🚀
In real-world DevOps, it’s not enough to just deploy — we must also monitor, analyze, and respond to system behavior.

🔹 Why Monitoring is Important in GitOps
 Even though GitOps automates deployments, we still need to:
Track application health
Detect failures quickly
Ensure system performance
This is where monitoring tools come into play.

🔹 Prometheus
 Prometheus is widely used for metrics collection in Kubernetes.
Collects real-time metrics
Stores time-series data
Helps track system performance

🔹 Grafana
 Grafana is used for visualizing metrics.
Creates dashboards
Displays graphs and insights
Helps teams understand system behavior easily

🔹 Alerts
 Monitoring is incomplete without alerts.
Trigger notifications on failures
Alert on high CPU, memory, or downtime
Helps teams respond quickly to issues

🔹 Real DevOps Flow
 GitOps Tool → Deploys application
 Prometheus → Collects metrics
 Grafana → Visualizes data
 Alerts → Notify issues

💡 Key Insight:
 Monitoring ensures your GitOps system is not just automated, but also observable, reliable, and production-ready.
